    "description": "Artist Unknown\nFramed Blue Agate Slab Wall Art\nAgate Slice with Gilt Edge on Matting\n20\" x 20\" x 2\"\nUnsigned\nThis contemporary wall display showcases a polished natural agate slab with banding in deep ocean blue, cerulean, and soft white. Accented along its perimeter with textured gold metallic leaf, the slice is mounted against a layered textured mat within a modern shadow box frame, blending organic geological beauty with clean architectural styling.\nNatural polished agate specimen featuring hand-applied gilt perimeter edging\nContemporary shadow box frame with natural woodgrain and white inner liner\nOuter frame measures 20\" x 20\" with mounting bracket attached to reverse\nCondition:\nVery good pre-owned condition. Agate specimen and glass are clean and undamaged. Inner frame liner shows minor surface scuffing upon close inspection, and backing board remains secure.\nNOTE\n: Unless otherwise indicated, this is a\nUSED\n, donated item/lot. We take every effort to document the condition and visible cosmetic damages, though we are not subject matter experts and items may contain unseen flaws or imperfections, such as cracks, crazing, bowing or separation.\nIf you have any questions regarding an item,\nplease reach out to us before placing your bid\n. If applicable, any testing for power or functionality, servicing or cleaning will be mentioned within the listing. Please assume items are untested, unserviced and presented as pictured otherwise.\nJEWELRY\n: Gemstones have been tested with Presidium Gemstone Tester. Precious metals are tested with a Thermo Scientific Niton DXL. Testing results are included in our listings where applicable. Gold JSP solution & rare earth magnets may also be used in testing. Gemstones may be natural or lab created. We identify gemstones to the best of our ability and testing equipment, but\nwe cannot guarantee specific gemstones\nif they look or test similar to other stones. Sterling Silver items may have very slight or localized magnetic properties due to rhodium plating, non-silver components such as pins or springs in clasps, or dependent on the metal the silver was alloyed with. Watch condition and functionality will be documented when possible. Watches may otherwise not be running, have internal issues or need additional cleaning.\nPlease Note\n: Certain jewelry items and lots may experience tangling from the sorting and shipping process.\nAS-IS\n: Listings are sold\nAS-IS with no refunds for condition or functionality\n. This includes, but is not limited to all electronic listings, all card lots, all jewelry lots and grab bags.\nIf you have any questions regarding an item,\nplease reach out to us before placing your bid\n.\nCOMBINED SHIPPING\n: All Jewelry items can not be combined with other any other items, including other Jewelry items without contacting customer service before payment. We reserve the right to approve or deny combination of items for shipment at our discretion.",
